Project idea: TaskForge – Multi-Tenant Project Management & Time Tracking SaaS
You’ll build a backend for teams to manage projects, tasks, time logs, billing plans, and reports. Perfect for a full-stack portfolio.

Below is only the Django backend roadmap, split by weeks and days.

WEEK 1 – Project Skeleton & Core Architecture

Goal: Clean Django/DRF base, multi-app structure, config ready.

Day 1

Create repo and virtualenv.

Install Django, djangorestframework, python-dotenv.

Create project taskforge with core app.

Day 2

Set up settings modules: settings/base.py, settings/dev.py, settings/prod.py.

Configure DB (Postgres), INSTALLED_APPS, DRF defaults (pagination, auth, etc.).

Day 3

Create apps: accounts, workspaces, projects.

Wire them in INSTALLED_APPS.

Day 4

Create base models in core (TimeStampedModel, UUIDModel).

Apply first migration, test runserver.

Day 5

Configure urls.py for API prefix /api/v1/.

Install & set up drf-spectacular (or drf-yasg) for schema.

Day 6

Add simple healthcheck endpoint /api/health/.

Add basic docker-compose.yml for Postgres (no Dockerfile yet).

Day 7

Clean folder structure, add .env.example, .gitignore, and basic README.

WEEK 2 – Users, Auth, Roles (Accounts)

Goal: Custom user model, JWT auth, basic roles.

Day 1

Implement CustomUser (email login, no username) in accounts.models.

Update AUTH_USER_MODEL, migrate.

Day 2

Install SimpleJWT.

Configure JWT settings, token lifetime, custom claims (e.g., workspace info later).

Day 3

Implement register and login API with DRF views/serializers.

Return access + refresh tokens.

Day 4

Add UserProfile model (full_name, avatar, job_title, timezone).

Serializer + GET/PUT /me/ endpoint.

Day 5

Roles: add role field to user (admin, member) OR separate Role model.

Ensure superuser creation works.

Day 6

Add basic password reset stubs (no email yet): request + confirm endpoints.

Day 7

Write tests for registration, login, /me.

Fix edge cases (duplicate email, weak password).

WEEK 3 – Workspaces & Membership

Goal: Multi-tenant structure (teams/companies).

Day 1

Models in workspaces: Workspace, WorkspaceMembership.

Fields: name, slug, owner, plan, is_active.

Day 2

WorkspaceMembership: user, workspace, role, invited_by, status.

Day 3

Endpoints:

List user workspaces

Create workspace

Switch active workspace (store in user or via header).

Day 4

Invitation flow (basic):

POST /workspaces/{id}/invite/ (email + role).

accept_invite stub (token later).

Day 5

Permissions: ensure all project/task endpoints will be filtered by current workspace.

Add custom DRF permission class IsWorkspaceMember.

Day 6

Add middleware or util to resolve “current workspace” from header/URL.

Day 7

Tests for workspace creation, membership, permissions.

WEEK 4 – Projects & Kanban Tasks

Goal: Projects, columns, tasks, comments.

Day 1

Models in projects:

Project (workspace, name, description, status).

ProjectMembership (optional if per-project roles).

Day 2

Kanban:

TaskStatus (Backlog, In Progress, Done, …).

Task (project, title, description, assignee, status, priority, due_date, estimate_hours).

Day 3

Task extras:

Tag model + m2m with Task.

TaskComment (task, author, body).

Day 4

DRF ViewSets:

Project CRUD

Task CRUD

Filter tasks by status, assignee, due_date.

Day 5

Add search & ordering for tasks (title, created_at, priority).

Pagination tuning.

Day 6

Permissions:

Only workspace members can access.

Optional: project-level roles (owner, collaborator).

Day 7

Tests for project & task APIs.

WEEK 5 – Time Tracking & Reports

Goal: Time logs per task; reporting endpoints.

Day 1

TimeEntry model:

user, task, project, started_at, ended_at, duration, note.

Day 2

Endpoints:

Log time for a task (manual).

List time entries by task/user/project.

Day 3

Aggregation endpoints:

Total hours per project (date range).

Total hours per user (date range).

Day 4

Add constraints:

No negative durations.

Prevent overlapping entries (basic check).

Day 5

Reporting API:

/reports/summary/ – summarise hours per project/user.

Day 6

Optimize queries with select_related / prefetch_related.

Day 7

Tests for time tracking & reports.

WEEK 6 – Billing, Plans, & Stripe Integration

Goal: SaaS billing structure + basic Stripe.

Day 1

Models in billing app:

Plan (name, price_monthly, price_yearly, max_users, max_projects).

Subscription (workspace, plan, status, current_period_end, stripe_customer_id, stripe_sub_id).

Day 2

Assign default Free plan on workspace creation.

Enforce simple limits in code (e.g., max projects).

Day 3

Integrate Stripe SDK:

Create customer for workspace owner.

Create checkout session endpoint.

Day 4

Webhook endpoint /stripe/webhook/:

Handle subscription created/updated/canceled.

Day 5

Update Subscription on webhook events.

Day 6

Add endpoint to retrieve current subscription & plan limits.

Day 7

Tests with mocked Stripe calls.

WEEK 7 – Notifications & Activity Logs

Goal: Track activity; email & in-app notifications.

Day 1

ActivityLog model:

workspace, user, action_type, metadata (JSON), created_at.

Day 2

Hook into signals:

On Task create/update, Project create, TimeEntry log → create ActivityLog.

Day 3

Simple Notification model:

user, title, body, read_at, related_object (GenericForeignKey).

Day 4

Email backend setup (console in dev).

Utility function send_notification_email.

Day 5

When user is assigned to a task → create notification + send email.

Day 6

APIs:

List notifications

Mark as read

Day 7

Tests + ensure logs/notifications are filtered by workspace.

WEEK 8 – Permissions, Security & Throttling

Goal: Harden backend.

Day 1

Add per-object permissions (e.g., only creator or assignee can edit a task).

Custom DRF permissions.

Day 2

Add DRF throttling for login, register, and key endpoints.

Day 3

Implement audit logging for sensitive actions (billing, workspace changes).

Day 4

Ensure no data leaks across workspaces (extra tests).

Day 5

Rate-limit Stripe endpoints and webhooks.

Day 6

Security headers & CORS settings for future React client.

Day 7

Security test pass (manual checks, some automated tests).

